    description: >-
      Zenodo concept DOI. Always resolves to the latest
      archived version.
abstract: >-
  A first-principles model of a counterflow wet cooling tower,
  coupled to an ion-association water-chemistry engine, that
  evaluates each scale-forming mineral at the temperature where
  it is least soluble: calcite, gypsum and magnesium silicate at
  the hot condenser tube skin, amorphous silica at the cold tower
  basin. Six acceptance criteria were fixed and printed before
  fitting and scored on a campaign-wise holdout of published
  experimental data, re-scored once with thresholds unchanged after
  duplicated rows were found in the published data. Three pass and
  three fail; the failures are reported as failures and no threshold
  was moved. Includes
  an independent MATLAB and Simulink re-implementation agreeing
  with the Python core to 1.4e-5 K, and a register of the defects
  found in the authors' own work, each with the result it moved.
keywords:
  - cooling tower
  - district cooling
  - condenser water
  - water treatment
  - scale prediction
  - thermodynamics
  - process control
  - reproducible research
